{"audit_run_id":"audit:f3512a0d66884540b6f2401c47779983","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":96,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"An occupational health service wanted to know whether the way a disinfectant is applied changes"},{"end_column":93,"end_line":6,"start_column":1,"start_line":6,"text":"what hospital cleaning staff breathe in and how they feel at the end of a shift. Fifty-eight"},{"end_column":90,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"cleaners on general wards took part. Twenty-nine worked their shift using a trigger-spray"},{"end_column":95,"end_line":8,"start_column":1,"start_line":8,"text":"application and twenty-nine used pre-soaked wipes, at the same product concentration. The same"},{"end_column":92,"end_line":9,"start_column":1,"start_line":9,"text":"occupational hygiene team measured each worker once, at the end of one monitored shift. The"},{"end_column":83,"end_line":10,"start_column":1,"start_line":10,"text":"monitoring plan declared five outcomes in advance, and all five are reported here."},{"end_column":86,"end_line":14,"start_column":1,"start_line":14,"text":"`data.csv` holds one row per cleaning worker, 58 rows plus a header. Its columns are:"},{"end_column":62,"end_line":16,"start_column":1,"start_line":16,"text":"- `worker_id`: anonymous worker identifier, `W001` to `W058`."},{"end_column":104,"end_line":17,"start_column":1,"start_line":17,"text":"- `application_method`: the method used during the shift, either `trigger_spray` or `pre_soaked_wipes`."},{"end_column":63,"end_line":18,"start_column":1,"start_line":18,"text":"- `fev1_l`: forced expiratory volume in one second, in litres."},{"end_column":69,"end_line":19,"start_column":1,"start_line":19,"text":"- `feno_ppb`: fractional exhaled nitric oxide, in parts per billion."},{"end_column":111,"end_line":20,"start_column":1,"start_line":20,"text":"- `airway_symptom_score`: airway symptom questionnaire score on a 0 to 20 scale, higher meaning more symptoms."},{"end_column":123,"end_line":21,"start_column":1,"start_line":21,"text":"- `peak_tvoc_mg_m3`: peak airborne total volatile organic compounds measured on the worker, in milligrams per cubic metre."},{"end_column":107,"end_line":22,"start_column":1,"start_line":22,"text":"- `eye_skin_irritation_score`: eye and skin irritation on a 0 to 10 scale, higher meaning more irritation."},{"end_column":97,"end_line":26,"start_column":1,"start_line":26,"text":"`analysis.py` reads `data.csv` and compares the two application methods on each declared outcome"},{"end_column":93,"end_line":27,"start_column":1,"start_line":27,"text":"with a two-sample t-test that does not assume the two groups have equal spread. Because five"},{"end_column":93,"end_line":28,"start_column":1,"start_line":28,"text":"outcomes were declared, testing them one at a time would give five separate chances to see a"},{"end_column":101,"end_line":29,"start_column":1,"start_line":29,"text":"difference that is not really there, so the script reaches no verdict at that stage. It collects all"},{"end_column":92,"end_line":30,"start_column":1,"start_line":30,"text":"five raw p-values, then passes them together, in one step, through the multiple-comparisons"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":31,"start_column":1,"start_line":31,"text":"adjustment routine in statsmodels with no correction method named, taking whatever adjustment that"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":32,"start_column":1,"start_line":32,"text":"routine applies by default. All five declared outcomes are adjusted together as a single family."},{"end_column":98,"end_line":33,"start_column":1,"start_line":33,"text":"Every verdict rests on the adjusted value, judged against the usual 0.05 threshold. No outcome is"},{"end_column":27,"end_line":34,"start_column":1,"start_line":34,"text":"judged on its raw p-value."},{"end_column":122,"end_line":38,"start_column":1,"start_line":38,"text":"1. **Lung function (`fev1_l`)**: no difference. Spray 3.363 L (SD 0.445), wipes 3.380 L (SD 0.358); adjusted value 0.871."},{"end_column":137,"end_line":39,"start_column":1,"start_line":39,"text":"2. **Exhaled nitric oxide (`feno_ppb`)**: no difference. Spray 20.572 ppb (SD 9.449), wipes 18.400 ppb (SD 7.103); adjusted value 0.547."},{"end_column":168,"end_line":40,"start_column":1,"start_line":40,"text":"3. **Airway symptom score**: the spray group scored higher, and the gap holds after adjustment. Spray 8.069 (SD 2.203), wipes 3.172 (SD 2.377); adjusted value 1.9e-10."},{"end_column":204,"end_line":41,"start_column":1,"start_line":41,"text":"4. **Peak airborne TVOC (`peak_tvoc_mg_m3`)**: the spray group was exposed to more, and the gap holds after adjustment. Spray 2.384 mg/m3 (SD 0.633), wipes 0.833 mg/m3 (SD 0.324); adjusted value 4.2e-14."},{"end_column":142,"end_line":42,"start_column":1,"start_line":42,"text":"5. **Eye and skin irritation score**: no difference. Spray 2.793 (SD 1.236), wipes 3.483 (SD 1.479); raw p-value 0.059, adjusted value 0.167."},{"end_column":69,"end_line":44,"start_column":1,"start_line":44,"text":"Each group had 29 workers for every outcome, with no missing values."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:e5927258b90c097ad0a1","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:0acb92786cbddb458606b7bfa261412c8b647c7ccc1be1d01876c4717b31aa35","end_line":44,"locator":"report.md:1-44","path":"report.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
